  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1205 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nAs of noon CST, temperatures across the area are in the upper \n40s across most of the area, in the low 50s across south \ncentral SD. A cold front made its way across the area this \nmorning, leaving behind northerly winds at around 10 to 15 mph \nand cooler temperatures.\n\nHigh pressure will move in from the north through the rest of the \nday and into Thursday. This high starts to slowly move east Friday \nand by Saturday afternoon is centered over MN. Winds out of the \nsouth on the backside of the high will advect cooler air into the \narea and continue our cooler temps through Saturday. WAA takes over \nSunday and we start to warm up back towards the upper 40s to mid 50s \n(10 to 15 degrees above average). Low pressure begins to move \ntowards the area Tuesday from WY and enters western SD Wednesday. \nThis is still 7 days out, but there could be a chance for some \nprecipitation with this low pressure. \n\nHigh resolution models are showing some potential brief visibility \nreductions due to fog tonight, mainly west river. Visibilities are \nnot expected to be reduced a whole lot, maybe down to 2 miles. It \nwill be a little windy Friday through the weekend and into early \nnext work week. Friday through Sunday, winds will gust between 25 \nand 40 mph mainly west river with some spreading as far east as the \nJames River on Saturday. Monday, the highest gusts look to be in \nsouth central SD and around the Sisseton Hills. Tuesday, gusts \nbetween 30 and 35 mph will affect most of the CWA as the incoming \nlow fights with remaining high pressure.",
